    "scope": "Specific Temple of Hathor ruins within the mapped enclosure: two western rock-chapel entrance masses, open doorways, irregular tall/rounded/broken sandstone stela groups, low surviving wall remnants and fallen slabs around an open compound. No complete restored Egyptian temple, roofed court, full deciphered inscription or mine complex. Internal group counts, room fragments and chapel assignment to western map jogs are explicit photo/map-shape approximations rather than surveyed archaeology.",
    "identityBasis": "Exact-QID way580657250 is a mapped wall/archaeological extent about77.9x40m. It fixes center and undirected long axis; standard PMTiles named archaeological point35184952746082 corroborates the site. Native east/south at heading0; internal angle-0.452864836238rad. Western boundary jogs guide the approximate two chapel masses; picture-led internal groups and signed facing remain uncertain. A single independent native building about50m north stays unchanged.",
    "heightBasis": "Photo-led estimates: stelae1.6–4.9m, chapel portal/rock masses about3m, enclosure/wall remnants about0.5–1.3m. Thirty upright stones and thirty-eight fallen slabs express visible density, not a certified artifact inventory. Exact hieroglyphs, individual chips and buried rooms omitted.",
    "terrainBasis": "Pinned standard Protomaps2026-10-14/Mapzen13–14 extract. Retain original native six-meter plateau grid and the independent building. Long wall segments follow sampled grade; upright stelae and chapel portals use separately sampled local footings with buried bottoms. Coarse DEM cannot resolve exact plateau paving, rock-cave thresholds or archaeological levels; this is approximate above-ground visualization. No broad invented podium, terrain replacement or excavation cutout.",
